  "worked_solution": "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t) & =\u27e8{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,(6-{t}^{3}),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,({t}^{2}-6),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e86-{2}^{3},{2}^{2}-6,\\frac{2}{{2}^{3}}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-2,-2,\\frac{1}{4}\u27e9 \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 2}g(t) & =\u27e8{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,(5-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3-t)),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,\\sqrt{6-t},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\,(2t)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e85-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3-2),\\sqrt{6-2},2(2)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e85,2,4\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}[f(t)+g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t)+{lim}_{t\\to 2}g(t) \\\\  & =\u27e8-2,-2,\\frac{1}{4}\u27e9+\u27e85,2,4\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-2+5,-2+2,\\frac{1}{4}+4\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e83,0,\\frac{17}{4}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
